# Scene pass

When ori'el asks to cut a log, propose trunks, scene-pass, or "do what we did on OT-001 / OT-008":

1. Read and follow `.cursor/skills/scene-pass/SKILL.md` **before** writing cuts.
2. Full sequential read. No CIO, no 40-msg caps, no begin/mid/end trays.
3. Propose only (`scene_scenes` / `scene_logs` status `proposed`). They accept · edit.
4. Do not silently move existing `hand_cuts`. Explain seq disagreements; move only if asked.
5. Yard is archive. Compost writes live in `bench.db`. Do not commit unless asked.
6. After trunks exist, a second round proposes **soft tags on those trunks** (`hand_cuts.tags_json`), not the log. Do not overwrite tags they already wrote. Talk first, then do.
